diagnosis_text:
The BIND9 DNS server (`dns_server`, IP 10.200.0.2) is running but has `recursion no;` set in its options block in `/etc/bind/named.conf`. This single directive is the sole cause of the outage.

**Mechanism:** Client resolvers (e.g., `host_1_1_1_1` using `nameserver 10.200.0.2`) send standard recursive queries with the RD (Recursion Desired) flag set. When BIND receives a query with RD=1 and recursion is disabled, it returns `REFUSED` rather than answering — confirmed directly by `dig` returning `status: REFUSED` with `recursion requested but not available`. The zone file itself (`/etc/bind/db.local`) is completely intact with all `A` records 
